# Concurrent-session safety

Canonical protocol: `/Users/the1finix/Documents/GitHub/brain-box/agents/concurrent-session-safety.md`.

This repo hosts both the six-study E0xx research lane and the M001
multi-agent-ensemble program, which have run as **separate concurrent
Cursor sessions on the same working tree** (confirmed 2026-07-01: an
E011-E016 sweep session and an M001 v1/v2-reframe session both edited
`ai_context.md` and `EXPERIMENTS.md` in the same window). Git does not
protect you here: no branch divergence, just a race on one working tree,
and `git commit` can silently discard the other session's edits.

Before editing or committing any of `ai_context.md`, `EXPERIMENTS.md`,
`DATA_LEDGER.md`, or `programs/M001_multi_agent_ensemble/.../evolution_ledger.md`:

1. Re-read the file fresh immediately before editing — don't trust an
   earlier-session copy.
2. Prefer additive edits (new table row / new section) over rewriting an
   existing section.
3. Never `git add -A` / `git add .` — stage explicit paths only, and
   never sweep up files you don't recognize as your own session's work
   (e.g. another program's in-flight report template).
4. Before committing, run `git diff --cached <file>` and confirm every
   line is yours; unrecognized content means another session is active
   — stop and reconcile by hand, don't overwrite.
5. Commit in small units rather than one end-of-session batch.
6. Check `git log --oneline -5` at session start — a same-day commit
   from a program you're not touching is a signal another session may
   be live right now.

